      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Silver City is the birthplace of Hall of Famer Spencer Haywood, who won Olympic gold in 1968 and helped pioneer early NBA entry rules.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/Silver_City,_Mississippi",
      "category": "people",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Early settlement in the area drew migrants to fertile Delta lands after the Civil War, with plantation farming and freed African Americans shaping its early community.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/Silver_City,_Mississippi",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Located in central Humphreys County, Silver City sits on the Mississippi Delta’s fertile plains, just west of the Yazoo River.",
